<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - BG Bank sees lower Danish '97 c/a surplus.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - BG Bank sees lower Danish '97 c/a surplus.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Denmark's third biggest BG Bank on Thursday halved its expectations for Denmark's 1997 current account surplus to four billion crowns from eight billion crowns in its last forecast in October 1996.</p>
<p>At the same time it lowered its inflation forecast for this year to 2.5 percent from 2.6 percent, leaving its estimate for GDP (gross domestic product) growth unchanged at three percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in December foresaw 2.9 percent GDP growth, 2.3 percent inflation, 8.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 13.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>BG Bank (2/97)	3.0    2.5	  7.9	    4.0</p>
<p>NatWest (2/97)	3.0    2.6	  8.2	    8.3</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs(1/97) 3.5    2.6	  8.1	   10.7</p>
<p>HSBC/Capel (1/97)   2.8    2.5	  8.3	    1.0</p>
<p>M. Grenfell (1/97)  2.8    2.3	  8.4	   13.0</p>
<p>Codan Bank (1/97)   2.8    2.25	 7.7	   13.5</p>
<p>CSFB (1/97)	   2.9    2.1	  --	     --</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch (1/97)2.4    2.3	  9.0	   20.0</p>
<p>Danske Bank(12/96)  2.75   2.25	 8.0	   14.1</p>
<p>Citibank (12/96)    2.9    2.4	  8.2	   15.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
